   "id": 667627,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>For questions 1 - 5, use the the three exponential functions defined below:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><span data-math=\"f(x)=100 \\cdot 3^x\">f(x)=100 \\cdot 3^x</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"g(x)=100 \\cdot (3.5)^x\">g(x)=100 \\cdot (3.5)^x</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"h(x)=100 \\cdot 4^x\">h(x)=100 \\cdot 4^x</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\">\n  <li>Which of these functions grows the least quickly?</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1331778,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"h(x)\"></span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1331779,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"g(x)\"></span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1331780,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"f(x)\"></span>"
    }
   ],
